  "brief": "Two-and-a-half-storey dark brick house in the East Ferry Avenue district, converted in the 1930s to a sanitarium by Detroit's first Black radiologist: a hipped roof with a gabled front dormer and a shingled front gable, a small classical entrance porch with a balcony above and brick walls. Stands among similar big brick houses facing a lawn strip and street trees.",
